#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186156929 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c4234a-3aa1-5b6b-b68b-48e6aa2b0dfb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function Given Its First Derivative"}] :question/id #uuid "332b1d25-852f-51ad-9a38-62b562ae247f" :question/math-academy-id "e-12522" :question/problem "Find $\\boldsymbol f''(\\pi,0)$ for the function $f(x,y)$ given that\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/assets/08502aa81729d4f88aec094e2e2f5c7b4a57825ef3767f1eec29700ceb6e21a3.png)" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f: \\mathbb R^n \\to \\mathbb R,$ given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/assets/025dd1a0b89b52e32a3e42e5bd3492261ed060f104f627051b6950c7f94d66c1.png)\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/assets/f1a47569220f01e1dc474a13a5040e969449ee0b10cfe7df39c3aec4c6175f41.png)\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/assets/f0b46d26ccc6fefc404b021bde11c4d6959c00ae0ef1145a9984da602bcc54ef.png)\n\nFirst, notice that since ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/assets/964f8ac9ca9c305faef8562f66d063f318ecbe402df337377bd9efdf61301567.png) \n we must have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x} = e^y\\cos x ,  \n\\qquad \n\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y} =e^y\\sin x .\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)=-{e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)={e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)={e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)={e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & {e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ {e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & {e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate this matrix at $(\\pi,0).$ This gives\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/assets/540c920abd2989b29aae275eedd179c5118e82354915e591c0d1c5296ca9fa21.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186156930 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "037ff08b-3246-5eed-870b-b4951f319c96" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Hessian Determinant"}] :question/id #uuid "53ca572c-798a-5529-9702-df3291a2b500" :question/math-academy-id "e-12523" :question/problem "Given that \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/assets/b3e96b1a54af842b69da4ae5fcb44858bffdac48b27cde6677c15c05906e890d.png) \n evaluate the Hessian determinant of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(0,1).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f: \\mathbb R^n \\to \\mathbb R,$ given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/assets/af5524049f5f8b3c4c4241520f2d874b454d61b1b025362f5193437f766e610b.png)\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/assets/8882516e2732e419efdfb8439265212dd4f380d6a6ea58f6ff1291030bf50bfb.png)\n\nThe Hessian determinant $H(x,y)$ is the determinant of the second derivative:\n\n$$\nH(\\mathbf x) = \\det \\left( \\boldsymbol{f}''(\\mathbf x) \\right)\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/assets/4fede2bb5c2306f62b55b7996488baee52c69e7d41b011e0e9d2b7405e63a8f4.png)\n\nFirst, notice that since ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/assets/9252d1ce4f5df828f45351d01e0709cf2f2ca5df2c9c25390c111f40ca00fb22.png) we must have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x} = \\ln y, \n\\qquad \n\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y} = \\dfrac xy.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)=0\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{x}{y})=\\frac{1}{y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)=\\frac{1}{y}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{x}{y})=-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & \\frac{1}{y} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & -\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(0,1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(0,1)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nH(0,1) = 0 \\cdot 0 - 1\\cdot 1 = -1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186156931 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ddf99849-1f2b-5c34-828c-164ad4058c92" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function"}] :question/id #uuid "235325ea-4a42-5f63-974a-edd459a4a771" :question/math-academy-id "e-12524" :question/problem "Find $\\boldsymbol f''(1,0)$ for the function $f(x,y)  = x^2 e^y.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f: \\mathbb R^n \\to \\mathbb R,$ given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/assets/7444a8128c085d7bf4f56a57a60c260864a50da0b744b6dbe22a2ced89a0588d.png)\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/assets/22dd960829ea268e5aade685b56949f8998f87ae8c040a90f04436cbfc6b9a58.png)\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/assets/4fede2bb5c2306f62b55b7996488baee52c69e7d41b011e0e9d2b7405e63a8f4.png)\n\nFirst, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{e}^{y}) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{e}^{y})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2x{e}^{y} & {x}^{2}{e}^{y}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x\\text{ }\\,{e}^{y})=2\\text{ }\\,{e}^{y}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{e}^{y})=2x\\text{ }\\,{e}^{y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x\\text{ }\\,{e}^{y})=2x\\text{ }\\,{e}^{y}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{e}^{y})={x}^{2}{e}^{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\text{ }\\,{e}^{y} & 2x\\text{ }\\,{e}^{y} \\\\ 2x\\text{ }\\,{e}^{y} & {x}^{2}{e}^{y}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate this matrix at $\\left(1,0\\right).$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1,0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157471 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c4234a-3aa1-5b6b-b68b-48e6aa2b0dfb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function Given Its First Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "871283d2-1f9f-53d5-a229-b02b6a59bee4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153402} {:answer/id #uuid "9176a86f-7b1f-5dff-adea-fbfff8ce6aed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153403} {:answer/id #uuid "c90476f1-09e0-5ef7-91ae-e5822686aaa4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153404} {:answer/id #uuid "fb03cb9c-b8af-518f-ae3f-6a83142bec0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153405} {:answer/id #uuid "2f28fe91-990f-5a32-b4fc-2e24861f3c1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153406}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb03cb9c-b8af-518f-ae3f-6a83142bec0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153405} :answer-field/id #uuid "42b7b11e-e967-5e86-b1e5-589356b1084d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153401}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3b064463-cab9-5bec-b4bd-67252dafbaa5" :question/math-academy-id "q-102477" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(1,2)$ for the function $f(x,y)$ given that\n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}y-2xy & x-{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}y-2xy & x-{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}],$ \n we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=y-2xy,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x-{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y-2xy)=-2y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x-{x}^{2})=1-2x \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y-2xy)=1-2x\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x-{x}^{2})=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}-2y & 1-2x \\\\ 1-2x & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate this matrix at $(1,2).$ This gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(1,2)=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364941 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "037ff08b-3246-5eed-870b-b4951f319c96" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Hessian Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15152ce0-2ad0-5fbe-8e02-7e363388b0c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-2{\\pi }^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364943} {:answer/id #uuid "3bf48c51-728d-5aa7-ba8f-f6181230d084" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{\\pi }^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364944} {:answer/id #uuid "6ebab16c-d020-56a6-8aa7-4657a8c695c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364945} {:answer/id #uuid "575b63e0-b224-5f63-81bf-770a43cd8a7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364946} {:answer/id #uuid "b6bc9658-5be2-5242-b8b6-0c28a7e886c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\pi }^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "575b63e0-b224-5f63-81bf-770a43cd8a7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364946} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc8bc93e-e92d-561c-8f69-7e91b3d1ec9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364942}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "64d88488-c131-5b90-b996-0433a97d3737" :question/math-academy-id "q-102688" :question/problem "Given that \n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy) & x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}],$ \nevaluate the Hessian determinant of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(\\pi ,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe Hessian determinant $H(x,y)$ is the determinant of the second derivative:\n\n$$\nH(x)=det({f}^{″}(x))\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since\n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy) & x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}],$\nwe must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy),\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))=-{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy) \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))=-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy) & -{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(\\pi ,-1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(\\pi ,-1)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nH(\\pi ,-1)=0\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot (-1)=-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364948 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c4234a-3aa1-5b6b-b68b-48e6aa2b0dfb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function Given Its First Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d83017a8-d7a0-5257-b688-8e0e64ba9fa5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364950} {:answer/id #uuid "4bb702c3-4bc2-500d-9c16-cbc6f3ec65f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364951} {:answer/id #uuid "cca141ca-493d-5423-b6c7-3670a4139cf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364952} {:answer/id #uuid "b194eb44-7cd0-5bd3-9250-1f32b2777399" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364953} {:answer/id #uuid "76fbf3c6-4c4d-5502-bafd-69c9184cc1f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364954}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4bb702c3-4bc2-500d-9c16-cbc6f3ec65f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364951} :answer-field/id #uuid "971f1dc6-0ce8-502e-9a46-f6fe020466ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364949}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f5b90395-91d4-59c1-9c6f-afa662efbb91" :question/math-academy-id "q-163635" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(2,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ for the function $f(x,y)$ given that\n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & {x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & {x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}],$ \n we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)=2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)=2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)=-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\ 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y & -{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate this matrix at $(2,\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ This gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(2,\\frac{\\pi }{2})=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364955 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c4234a-3aa1-5b6b-b68b-48e6aa2b0dfb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function Given Its First Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50f86f66-ae94-5851-ba33-ab57d53ee22e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}20 & -5 \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364957} {:answer/id #uuid "28822fbd-5c58-5060-88c5-88e697415346" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 20 \\\\ 20 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364958} {:answer/id #uuid "5b5fcded-c5b9-5534-b96b-d771d791e7b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 10 \\\\ 10 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364959} {:answer/id #uuid "983d88c0-d87c-5dd3-a41c-72fdaaf93edf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364960} {:answer/id #uuid "9232dbae-a74a-5820-a223-5cd2a6873852" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364961}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9232dbae-a74a-5820-a223-5cd2a6873852" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364961} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ef2bc12-5fc1-5ae0-b2f4-298237b52419" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364956}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "80f3f97d-e5ae-5fea-a537-3ca9f7c75a2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-163637" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2})$ for the function $f(x,y)$ given that\n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}10xy & 5{x}^{2}-2y\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}10xy & 5{x}^{2}-2y\\end{aligned}],$ \n we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=10xy,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=5{x}^{2}-2y.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(10xy)=10y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(5{x}^{2}-2y)=10x \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(10xy)=10x\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(5{x}^{2}-2y)=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}10y & 10x \\\\ 10x & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate this matrix at $(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2}).$ This gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2})=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364962 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "037ff08b-3246-5eed-870b-b4951f319c96" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Hessian Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0553436a-ec9f-5614-a3a7-bdef480e67c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364964} {:answer/id #uuid "3d86b3bd-73e9-56b6-bde9-47251d1bde60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364965} {:answer/id #uuid "146ce674-f89a-5f0b-be2d-ff21383cd3b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "81" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364966} {:answer/id #uuid "d8eb4341-13b3-55b6-bfaa-b10a5e33651d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364967} {:answer/id #uuid "086f16c6-22fe-51f4-85cf-f32133653e3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364968}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d86b3bd-73e9-56b6-bde9-47251d1bde60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364965} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdda514b-afcd-588e-8bc0-3432137e78eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364963}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d964405d-0ccf-53d6-bbf6-1a3a2c9a145e" :question/math-academy-id "q-163641" :question/problem "Given that \n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}+6x-4y & 4{y}^{3}-4x+8y\\end{aligned}],$ \nevaluate the Hessian determinant of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(1,0).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe Hessian determinant $H(x,y)$ is the determinant of the second derivative:\n\n$$\nH(x)=det({f}^{″}(x))\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since\n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}+6x-4y & 4{y}^{3}-4x+8y\\end{aligned}],$\nwe must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=3{x}^{2}+6x-4y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=4{y}^{3}-4x+8y.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{x}^{2}+6x-4y)=6x+6\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4{y}^{3}-4x+8y)=-4 \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{x}^{2}+6x-4y)=-4\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4{y}^{3}-4x+8y)=12{y}^{2}+8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6x+6 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 12{y}^{2}+8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(1,0),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1,0)=[\\begin{aligned}12 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nH(1,0)=12\\cdot 8-(-4)\\cdot (-4)=80.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364969 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "037ff08b-3246-5eed-870b-b4951f319c96" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Hessian Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4223c84a-633e-5d34-ae57-21c4f7de5091" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364971} {:answer/id #uuid "02349ac6-0b22-5fb1-8e57-19399fecf3f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364972} {:answer/id #uuid "e27acc18-d276-599f-b725-1840f8eb24ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364973} {:answer/id #uuid "b4f1b36e-b82e-52a3-99d4-bd6f57fbe987" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364974} {:answer/id #uuid "2a0c6bec-1135-5071-931f-2dc14d4eb0b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364975}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e27acc18-d276-599f-b725-1840f8eb24ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364973} :answer-field/id #uuid "6aae77dd-804e-5791-9b66-5a8e698e4c7f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364970}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2c30dd99-4223-5fc5-b0a9-d42d9d800191" :question/math-academy-id "q-163642" :question/problem "Given that \n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}4xy-3{y}^{2} & 2{x}^{2}-6xy\\end{aligned}],$ \nevaluate the Hessian determinant of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe Hessian determinant $H(x,y)$ is the determinant of the second derivative:\n\n$$\nH(x)=det({f}^{″}(x))\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since\n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}4xy-3{y}^{2} & 2{x}^{2}-6xy\\end{aligned}],$\nwe must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=4xy-3{y}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2{x}^{2}-6xy.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4xy-3{y}^{2})=4y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}-6xy)=4x-6y \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4xy-3{y}^{2})=4x-6y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{x}^{2}-6xy)=-6x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4y & 4x-6y \\\\ 4x-6y & -6x\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(1,1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1,1)=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nH(1,1)=4\\cdot (-6)-(-2)\\cdot (-2)=-28.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364976 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "037ff08b-3246-5eed-870b-b4951f319c96" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Hessian Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c83cccde-cf73-5a05-8d0c-b262a28012e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364978} {:answer/id #uuid "104e3f2a-664f-5856-a8d6-31e370a4a310" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364979} {:answer/id #uuid "c2802d60-5247-5d5e-8a1f-c78e7d7317aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364980} {:answer/id #uuid "4442e0f5-b1ca-5665-ba7a-9aaf69712685" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364981} {:answer/id #uuid "66c64587-d6fa-58df-8e6e-e1b02ffd7246" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364982}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66c64587-d6fa-58df-8e6e-e1b02ffd7246" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364982} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f1273e2-fc4a-5ad6-89c3-cbf4d4013717" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364977}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e48899df-ddb7-5496-b3bb-6235b45449a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-163643" :question/problem "Given that \n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y-x) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y)+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-y)\\end{aligned}],$ \nevaluate the Hessian determinant of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(\\pi ,\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe Hessian determinant $H(x,y)$ is the determinant of the second derivative:\n\n$$\nH(x)=det({f}^{″}(x))\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since\n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y-x) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y)+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-y)\\end{aligned}],$\nwe must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y-x),\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y)+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-y).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y-x))=-y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y)\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y)+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-y))=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y-x)+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y) \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y-x))=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y-x)+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y)\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y)+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-y))=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-y)-y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(y-x)+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(y-x)+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y) & 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-y)-y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(\\pi ,\\pi ),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(\\pi ,\\pi )=[\\begin{aligned}-\\pi  & \\pi  \\\\ \\pi  & -\\pi \\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nH(\\pi ,\\pi )=(-\\pi )\\cdot (-\\pi )-\\pi \\cdot \\pi =0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157729 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ddf99849-1f2b-5c34-828c-164ad4058c92" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae64ecf2-f100-5ee1-bf22-d62f17c06d20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}y\\cos x & 0 \\\\ 0 & -x\\sin y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155627} {:answer/id #uuid "195c549d-45b4-55f3-a403-f4ee843b6e1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & \\cos y + 1 \\\\ \\cos y + 1 & -x\\sin y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155628} {:answer/id #uuid "30a4bd7f-a653-586c-8d6c-48bbd5f3eadf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & \\cos y + x \\\\ \\cos y + x & \\sin y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155629} {:answer/id #uuid "6b54a19a-e583-584b-a065-7c3d2342cae8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & \\cos y + 1 \\\\ \\cos y + 1 & x\\cos y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155630} {:answer/id #uuid "7613ab91-83d0-595d-baf0-b61833c485f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}y\\cos x & 1 \\\\ 1 & -x\\sin y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "195c549d-45b4-55f3-a403-f4ee843b6e1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & \\cos y + 1 \\\\ \\cos y + 1 & -x\\sin y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155628} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f160e6d-8669-5f1d-a718-6927812f7f8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155626}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1fc495d4-08fa-5ada-9f41-a42761e42726" :question/math-academy-id "q-80939" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(x,y)$ for the function $f(x,y)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+xy.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+xy) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+xy)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+y & x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+x\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+y)=0\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+1 \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+1\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+x)=-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & \\operatorname{cos}⁡y+1 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡y+1 & -x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364983 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ddf99849-1f2b-5c34-828c-164ad4058c92" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a959768f-f344-594d-b877-47fbec33620a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}{e}^{xy} & {e}^{xy} \\\\ {e}^{xy} & {x}^{2}{e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364985} {:answer/id #uuid "e0b58862-d09a-52a2-a26c-755afa039661" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}{e}^{xy} & {e}^{xy}(1+xy) \\\\ {e}^{xy}(1+xy) & {x}^{2}{e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364986} {:answer/id #uuid "db485220-6bfd-53d3-a20a-3c70e88501e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{xy} & {e}^{xy}+xy \\\\ {e}^{xy}+xy & {e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364987} {:answer/id #uuid "c5646e33-2662-5a2e-a68e-5dff25f92833" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}{e}^{xy} & {e}^{xy}(2+xy) \\\\ {e}^{xy}(2+xy) & {y}^{2}{e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364988} {:answer/id #uuid "c06664ed-c82e-58ec-b253-08acbeb1b049" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{xy} & {e}^{xy}(1+xy) \\\\ {e}^{xy}(1+xy) & {e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0b58862-d09a-52a2-a26c-755afa039661" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}{e}^{xy} & {e}^{xy}(1+xy) \\\\ {e}^{xy}(1+xy) & {x}^{2}{e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364986} :answer-field/id #uuid "f062014e-da95-5e90-80f7-697c9690531e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364984}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5b55b18c-139d-56b5-94eb-26aeb293ef39" :question/math-academy-id "q-80947" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(x,y)$ for the function $f(x,y)={e}^{xy}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{xy}) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{xy})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}y{e}^{xy} & x{e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y{e}^{xy})={y}^{2}{e}^{xy}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{e}^{xy})={e}^{xy}+xy\\,\\text{ }{e}^{xy} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y{e}^{xy})={e}^{xy}+xy\\,\\text{ }{e}^{xy}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{e}^{xy})={x}^{2}{e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}{e}^{xy} & {e}^{xy}(1+xy) \\\\ {e}^{xy}(1+xy) & {x}^{2}{e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364990 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c4234a-3aa1-5b6b-b68b-48e6aa2b0dfb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function Given Its First Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ce9f13c-d9d3-59ec-b2e3-7b6d7f7cff56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 6y\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364992} {:answer/id #uuid "6d0fde94-e7ae-5f10-ae5f-c18dcd5baf62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4x \\\\ 4x & -4y\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364993} {:answer/id #uuid "113be9ea-8239-5063-9d52-c790cdd779f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2y & 4x \\\\ 4x & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364994} {:answer/id #uuid "c7f47f8e-bdf6-582e-920b-c709d06a8bbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6y & 4x \\\\ 4x & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364995} {:answer/id #uuid "1213a6a8-21a5-5951-ac7b-333113736301" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2x & 6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364996}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ce9f13c-d9d3-59ec-b2e3-7b6d7f7cff56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 6y\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364992} :answer-field/id #uuid "984f5259-dc35-537b-950f-5d0aaafe85ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364991}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "52b9f18b-c40a-5c3f-88f5-e136ad636bb1" :question/math-academy-id "q-81009" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(x,y)$ for the function $f(x,y)$ given that\n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}-4y+1 & 3{y}^{2}-4x-1\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}-4y+1 & 3{y}^{2}-4x-1\\end{aligned}],$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-4y+1,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=3{y}^{2}-4x-1.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-4y+1)=0\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{y}^{2}-4x-1)=-4 \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-4y+1)=-4\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{y}^{2}-4x-1)=6y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 6y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364997 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "037ff08b-3246-5eed-870b-b4951f319c96" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Hessian Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a4a17d9-5f89-5d34-9bc9-7d4bc75a793c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364999} {:answer/id #uuid "bdb473b9-20da-57f8-9535-02cbb7ffd3a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365000} {:answer/id #uuid "afaa6d0a-c173-5b16-a7d6-7f98440e8b31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365001} {:answer/id #uuid "a12d57b7-d98e-5281-94b3-f397e642fe49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365002} {:answer/id #uuid "ed3ea629-c721-5520-9092-d2887191c1d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365003}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a12d57b7-d98e-5281-94b3-f397e642fe49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365002} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac66da5f-5af2-5ef4-853e-729ee2370ec7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364998}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "45ee04cf-eb55-5e8d-9a0d-295caa28fa48" :question/math-academy-id "q-81023" :question/problem "Given that \n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}2(x-1){y}^{2} & 2(x-1)^{2}y\\end{aligned}],$ \nevaluate the Hessian determinant of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(0,1).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe Hessian determinant $H(x,y)$ is the determinant of the second derivative:\n\n$$\nH(x)=det({f}^{″}(x))\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}2(x-1){y}^{2} & 2(x-1)^{2}y\\end{aligned}],$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2(x-1){y}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2(x-1)^{2}y.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2(x-1){y}^{2})=2{y}^{2}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2(x-1)^{2}y)=4(x-1)y \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2(x-1){y}^{2})=4(x-1)y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2(x-1)^{2}y)=2(x-1)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2{y}^{2} & 4(x-1)y \\\\ 4(x-1)y & 2(x-1)^{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(0,1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(0,1)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nH(0,1)=2\\cdot 2-(-4)\\cdot (-4)=-12.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365004 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c4234a-3aa1-5b6b-b68b-48e6aa2b0dfb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function Given Its First Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f87e09d9-b96e-57a2-a46b-0b86ee7e6c87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365006} {:answer/id #uuid "d00818d0-c5f2-5c89-a9a6-85860160f7c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{2-x} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365007} {:answer/id #uuid "b9c1ff1a-fedc-53bf-9bcd-d3bf24fff1d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-x} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365008} {:answer/id #uuid "6507c299-b466-526d-8287-f326a5e34d31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2-x} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365009} {:answer/id #uuid "fc8525c8-6d4c-51d5-b2d2-7572e1c44dc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}e & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365010}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6507c299-b466-526d-8287-f326a5e34d31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2-x} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365009} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0f2cb1a-ba6b-54f6-bade-4fd1d5107acf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365005}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4c1140cc-a082-5c3a-9371-31aefe906ee9" :question/math-academy-id "q-81110" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(x,y)$ for the function $f(x,y)$ given that\n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}e-{e}^{2-x} & 2y\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}e-{e}^{2-x} & 2y\\end{aligned}],$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=e-{e}^{2-x},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2y.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(e-{e}^{2-x})={e}^{2-x}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y)=0 \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(e-{e}^{2-x})=0\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2-x} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365011 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ddf99849-1f2b-5c34-828c-164ad4058c92" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7a24aa2-6613-5404-8b61-9f0360442eda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & 2{e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\ 2{e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & {e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365013} {:answer/id #uuid "0cebbac0-0da0-5dc7-afd9-ca1cc5b20538" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}(2+4{x}^{2}){e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & 4xy{e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\ 4xy{e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & (2+4{y}^{2}){e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365014} {:answer/id #uuid "815e2989-d2ac-53db-ac92-56a41c46a90a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}(2+4x){e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & 2{e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\ 2{e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & (2+4y){e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365015} {:answer/id #uuid "fa1874e9-0770-5f2d-a605-212a71f7c41a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}(2+4{x}^{2}){e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & 0 \\\\ 0 & (2+4{y}^{2}){e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365016} {:answer/id #uuid "cd92eb1f-bf56-52be-9e24-671ff930c874" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}(2+4{x}^{2}){e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & 2{e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\ 2{e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & (2+4{y}^{2}){e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365017}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0cebbac0-0da0-5dc7-afd9-ca1cc5b20538" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}(2+4{x}^{2}){e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & 4xy{e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\ 4xy{e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & (2+4{y}^{2}){e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365014} :answer-field/id #uuid "d30d1a2e-2166-5e0b-afbc-84c87bbefacb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365012}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "93f5f48f-d420-5aa1-920f-ebb239acb303" :question/math-academy-id "q-81111" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(x,y)$ for the function $f(x,y)={e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2x{e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & 2y{e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x{e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}})=(2+4{x}^{2}){e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y{e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}})=4xy{e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x{e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}})=4xy{e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y{e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}})=(2+4{y}^{2}){e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}(2+4{x}^{2}){e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & 4xy{e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\ 4xy{e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & (2+4{y}^{2}){e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365018 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ddf99849-1f2b-5c34-828c-164ad4058c92" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "686adeba-dae4-5d97-a60a-63cdb9ec1d29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2{y}^{2} & 4xy \\\\ 4xy & 2({x}^{2}-1)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365020} {:answer/id #uuid "a014e6fb-9047-5386-940e-8d6d00460928" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2y & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2({x}^{2}-1)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365021} {:answer/id #uuid "309a0585-e3b2-5b59-a649-089e97a86a3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2y & 2xy \\\\ 2xy & 2({x}^{2}-1)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365022} {:answer/id #uuid "ddd802c6-0729-5df3-a155-3d6ae8c8ce66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2y \\\\ 2y & 2({x}^{2}-1)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365023} {:answer/id #uuid "36d8011d-a00e-5381-9a6e-2a4cdad44313" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2y & 2x \\\\ 2x & 2({x}^{2}-1)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365024}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "686adeba-dae4-5d97-a60a-63cdb9ec1d29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2{y}^{2} & 4xy \\\\ 4xy & 2({x}^{2}-1)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365020} :answer-field/id #uuid "306146fd-2450-50f2-9d7c-01f25ac77438" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365019}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "953fe33f-1428-5dd9-88fe-de345ba3b466" :question/math-academy-id "q-81119" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(x,y)$ for the function $f(x,y)={y}^{2}({x}^{2}-1).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2}({x}^{2}-1)) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}({x}^{2}-1))\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2x{y}^{2} & 2y({x}^{2}-1)\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x{y}^{2})=2{y}^{2}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y({x}^{2}-1))=4xy \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x{y}^{2})=4xy\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y({x}^{2}-1))=2({x}^{2}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}2{y}^{2} & 4xy \\\\ 4xy & 2({x}^{2}-1)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365025 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ddf99849-1f2b-5c34-828c-164ad4058c92" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf275c60-709a-5dde-987d-70d9d909bf45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365027} {:answer/id #uuid "4e5aeef0-7c3b-5e26-963f-af5017f88979" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365028} {:answer/id #uuid "70abffe5-ca6b-5ec2-9c2a-79dd5da4e83e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365029} {:answer/id #uuid "adcaa052-6d7c-567e-af8f-3946c47a2e69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365030} {:answer/id #uuid "f43acab8-541f-56dd-bf48-2923951342b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365031}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "adcaa052-6d7c-567e-af8f-3946c47a2e69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365030} :answer-field/id #uuid "23cb1c28-fb05-56f5-a623-2400fdc9b744" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365026}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "74262592-fff9-55b8-b09e-a90c6c4a1e4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-81123" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(-1,2)$ for the function $f(x,y)=(y-1)({x}^{2}-1).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}((y-1)({x}^{2}-1)) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}((y-1)({x}^{2}-1))\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2x(y-1) & {x}^{2}-1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x(y-1))=2(y-1)\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-1)=2x \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x(y-1))=2x\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}-1)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}2(y-1) & 2x \\\\ 2x & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate this matrix at $(-1,2).$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(-1,2)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
